WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.807
James Sheldon Webb was born on April 11, 1943, in Arizona, while the United

2
00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:07.371
States was deep in the Second World War.

3
00:00:07.371 --> 00:00:12.306
His parents were James Wilford “Jay” Webb and Marion Beulah Brenay Webb. When

4
00:00:12.306 --> 00:00:17.050
Sheldon was born, they were living near the mill in a small one-room shack

5
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.921
with a lean-to kitchen. Marion remembered bitter cold, heavy snowstorms, and

6
00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:25.767
having to walk about a quarter mile just to reach their car.

7
00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:30.702
Beyond their small community, wartime America was transforming the Southwest.

8
00:00:30.702 --> 00:00:35.509
Troops and military equipment moved across Arizona, while scientists at Los

9
00:00:35.509 --> 00:00:40.509
Alamos, just across the state line in New Mexico, secretly developed the first

10
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:45.380
atomic weapons. In July 1945, when Sheldon was two, the Trinity test ushered

11
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.534
in the atomic age.

12
00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:51.533
The war touched Sheldon much more personally when Jay entered the Army. Marion

13
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:56.405
was left with young Sheldon, little money, and no car, and temporarily moved

14
00:00:56.405 --> 00:00:58.135
to stay with Jay’s parents.

15
00:00:58.135 --> 00:01:03.071
Then Sheldon became seriously ill with measles. Marion remembered him covered

16
00:01:03.071 --> 00:01:07.878
with red spots. His condition caused enough concern that Jay was allowed to

17
00:01:07.878 --> 00:01:10.249
come home briefly. Sheldon recovered.

18
00:01:10.249 --> 00:01:15.121
When Jay eventually returned from the war, Marion remembered Sheldon running

19
00:01:15.121 --> 00:01:17.236
down the road to meet his father.

20
00:01:17.236 --> 00:01:21.915
The postwar years were not immediately easy. Jay struggled to find steady

21
00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:26.594
work, and the family moved into an old house they repaired themselves. As

22
00:01:26.594 --> 00:01:31.529
Sheldon’s brothers and sisters arrived, the household grew around him. Family

23
00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:35.952
photographs preserve this period, including Sheldon together with his

24
00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:36.529
siblings.

25
00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:41.336
Meanwhile, Arizona was changing rapidly. Highways, automobiles, television,

26
00:01:41.336 --> 00:01:45.759
military installations, and Cold War technology were transforming the

27
00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:50.630
Southwest. Sheldon grew up between the older world of small-town Arizona and

28
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.155
the increasingly modern America emerging after the war.

29
00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:59.091
He graduated from high school in 1960. Soon afterward, Sheldon and his friend

30
00:01:59.091 --> 00:02:04.026
Kenny MacClaron went to California looking for work. Marion recalled that the

31
00:02:04.026 --> 00:02:06.974
two young men began considering the Air Force.

32
00:02:06.974 --> 00:02:11.653
Sheldon joined and served for about two years before receiving a hardship

33
00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:16.140
discharge that allowed him to return home and help his father. He then

34
00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.024
continued his education and attended college.

35
00:02:19.024 --> 00:02:23.896
In 1965, Sheldon married Inez Karen Prather, opening the next chapter of the

36
00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:25.049
Webb family story.

37
00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:29.921
Sheldon’s early life stretched from wartime Arizona through the beginning of

38
00:02:29.921 --> 00:02:34.792
the atomic age and the transformation of the postwar Southwest. Behind those

39
00:02:34.792 --> 00:02:39.663
enormous events was a more intimate story: a boy growing up amid separation,

40
00:02:39.663 --> 00:02:43.060
illness, hard work, family, and extraordinary change.

41
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.432
That is where Sheldon’s story begins.
